<title>USA: Portland Genl files Ore. open access pilot.</title>
<headline>Portland Genl files Ore. open access pilot.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, ORE. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portland General Electric Co, a wholly-owned  subisidiary of Enron Corp, said Friday it submitted plans to the Oregon  Public Utility Commission to allow customers in four communities a  choice of electricity providers.</p>
<p>The program accounts for about 15 percent of the utility's electrical  load.</p>
<p>If approved by the commission, customers could begin receiving electricity  from other suppliers by December.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761))</p>
